{"id": "EUVD-2026-103576", "enisaUuid": "b1b17377-7d02-32b0-9413-77fbf7926028", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: sr: enforce exact attribute length for SEG6_ATTR_DST\n\nIn seg6_genl_policy, SEG6_ATTR_DST is defined with .type = NLA_BINARY and\n.len = sizeof(struct in6_addr). For NLA_BINARY, .len only enforces the\nmaximum payload length and permits shorter payloads (e.g., 0 bytes).\nWhen seg6_genl_set_tunsrc() copies sizeof(struct in6_addr) bytes via\nkmemdup(val, sizeof(*val), GFP_KERNEL), a short SEG6_ATTR_DST attribute\ntriggers a 16-byte out-of-bounds read past skb->tail into uninitialized\nskb->head memory, which is stored in sdata->tun_src and leaked back to\nuserspace via SEG6_CMD_GET_TUNSRC.\n\nSwitch SEG6_ATTR_DST in seg6_genl_policy to\nNLA_POLICY_EXACT_LEN(sizeof(struct in6_addr)) so that generic netlink\nvalidation rejects any attribute whose length is not exactly\nsizeof(struct in6_addr) with -ERANGE.\n\nTested in QEMU against Linux 7.3.0-rc3 by sending a SEG6_CMD_SET_TUNSRC\nGeneric Netlink message with a 0-byte SEG6_ATTR_DST attribute followed\nby SEG6_CMD_GET_TUNSRC. On the unfixed kernel, SEG6_CMD_SET_TUNSRC\nsucceeds (err = 0) and SEG6_CMD_GET_TUNSRC leaks 16 bytes of\nuninitialized kernel heap memory (tun_src =\n836a61ecc4d25a1042a8d60411cfb378); with this patch applied,\nSEG6_CMD_SET_TUNSRC is rejected by netlink policy validation with\n-ERANGE (-34) and tun_src remains zeroed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/050a0aa3c80907b8c60a396b7e04d48d8b1a9e70", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/209eefebee54c4a5f01d68b61e8ac9881eca2de9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3ac68c1cdc2535d127b2bfd50c263d16c8e4199", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66bf65fa109326e4c4ddeb0b94093379f72838fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/195813bb7324c338eaba0aaa02b18681ee65b670", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fcfc362344edea745a69f3a705de50b731f3418", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94214cf0a08dd2c5f37aeeea46078d9dfe8e4a0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d959c75c27f90e9ec489d18ce5ee6b852ad4741"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98531", "GHSA-365h-h8v6-r47m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "043a4d72-e3f8-3908-b209-cf6269ff38ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "54beb23e-c99c-315a-aeaa-01e1aaa13c3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "915d7e5e5930b4f01d0971d93b9b25ed17d221aa <2d959c75c27f90e9ec489d18ce5ee6b852ad4741"}, {"id": "6ddac044-7c08-3260-bef8-6554c2102054", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "846d638f-c860-38fb-acf5-673885c08185", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "98a2a433-d3e3-3786-9812-1cb1441aff44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "915d7e5e5930b4f01d0971d93b9b25ed17d221aa <195813bb7324c338eaba0aaa02b18681ee65b670"}, {"id": "a22fb516-0b56-3884-bcfe-6b1c495099c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "915d7e5e5930b4f01d0971d93b9b25ed17d221aa <94214cf0a08dd2c5f37aeeea46078d9dfe8e4a0e"}, {"id": "a7985b0e-f424-3c88-b8b3-be89538f740e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "915d7e5e5930b4f01d0971d93b9b25ed17d221aa <e3ac68c1cdc2535d127b2bfd50c263d16c8e4199"}, {"id": "ac1b7882-f84d-3c99-8277-dde1fc6eb860", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "b3efcbfa-1f0c-32bb-89f7-f38dfee21cd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "915d7e5e5930b4f01d0971d93b9b25ed17d221aa <66bf65fa109326e4c4ddeb0b94093379f72838fd"}, {"id": "b9dd9b65-588b-3ac9-a991-8a02087c68c8", "pro